    "message": "Record a decision in Rust, and keep proposals as rows until something reads their object\n\nrules/decisions.rs: _propose_due returns ProposalRow and _observed_state ObservedRow, which answer\nwhat _apply_proposal's Python body reads. The new step _record_outcome writes the sink's row as JSON\nbytes, then commit_action and remember_decision, falling back rule by rule. The index reads the bytes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
